Z||000000||pherder||05-11-2001||08:00 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p84b70b81151a6a79d6a6f84cdccaf184/fe888c4a.jpg.orig.jpg"> <P>Purchased them from an old friend on the Fiero List.<P>Received them @ ~ 8 AM this morning!  The car (with the donor seats) was still at the service shop getting its A/C worked on.  Called the shop @ ~1 PM and was told it was ready.  Picked up the car, did some running around and got home ~ 3:30 PM.<BR> <BR>~ 3:45 PM started to unbolt the driver's seat.  ~4:45 finished bolting in the passenger's seat.  Yup, 1 hour to r&r both seats and put the covers on!  <P>I'm happy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||6
Z||000001||Jay||05-11-2001||08:06 PM||||Paul,  Looks good!!<BR> I always wanted to know this about Mr. Mike's seats.  First how much are they new and how good is the leather used?  The reason I ask is because I paid $400 for a cow hide that is Ferrari quality leather and then an additional $400 to have the seats reupholsterd.  Add a custom logo on the head rest and the total came up to $900 Canadian which is about $500 US.  Is Mr Mikes comparable to that in quality of leather and price?  My leather is so soft and yet it is durable.  How have the old (new to you seats held up?)<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||05-11-2001||08:40 PM||||Jay,<P>See  <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com</A>  for prices.  I don't think he will beat the prices you mention and they are cookie cutter style (i.e. the low priced ones ALL look alike!)<P>I had a set in my 86 GT/308 Kit car for ~ 3 years (black) and had <B>NO</B> problems with them.<P>What amazes me is getting them put on in such a quick time!  I have only done one other set (the 308 Kit Car) and that was 5 years ago!  I watched the tape he sends out one time a couple of nights ago and then went ahead and put them together.<P>As for how have they held up ... I believe these are 2-3 years old and they look like they have been barely used.  The original owner (Jason Wenglikowski) had them in his convertible that was on eBay last week.  He upgraded to a different color and did the rest of his interior with the same color leather so these seat covers became available.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||1
